From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:28:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 3226 appxdeploymentclient: staging, registering by name,
 users, state, status, integrity, cleanup, provisioning, App Installer files,
 cancelling

PackageManager did what AddPackageAsync and RemovePackageAsync need and answered
E_NOTIMPL to the rest.

 - StagePackageAsync (and the options, volume + optional and related set
   variants) extracts a package under WindowsApps without registering it: no
   alias, no Start menu entry, not found by the queries of the user;
   RegisterPackageByFullNameAsync registers a staged package (and what it was
   staged with); staging an installed package changes nothing.
 - FindUsers lists the users whose profile has the package (Staged or
   Installed), SetPackageState stores the state for all users (a tampered
   package's processes are ended), Package.Status reports it with the files
   and dependencies, VerifyContentIntegrityAsync checks the files against
   AppxBlockMap.xml (size and SHA-256 of each 64 KB block).
 - CleanupPackageForUserAsync takes a package away for a user, the files with
   it unless another user has the package (a removal also keeps the files of
   a package another user has); ProvisionPackageForAllUsersAsync marks the
   staged package of a family and registers it; StageUserDataAsync.
 - AddPackageByAppInstallerFileAsync reads an .appinstaller file (MainPackage,
   MainBundle, Dependencies, optional packages) and installs the packages.
 - IAsyncInfo::Cancel stops a deployment between two files (status Canceled,
   what was extracted taken away); the operation has its runtime class name.
 - AppListEntry.DisplayInfo gives the display name and description of the
   manifest and the logo as a stream reference.

